"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[6451],{29035:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"IsHidden","desc":"","params":[{"name":"root","desc":"A target root, or anything with `GetAttribute`.","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` when the root or its character carries `AI_HIDDEN = true`.","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":61,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"AliveRoots","desc":"Every player character with a Humanoid whose Health is above zero, by its root, minus the\\nones hidden with [Perception.HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTE]. The default `Targets` of every sense, so\\nhiding a player once hides them from Sight, Proximity and Watched together. Takes no\\narguments, so it can be a `Targets` function as it is.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The `HumanoidRootPart` of every player whose character is alive and not hidden.","lua_type":"{ BasePart }"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":109,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"AllAliveRoots","desc":"For the checks a hidden player still takes part in: [Perception.SeenByAnyone] uses it, since\\na player inside a locker can still see out of it.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"Every alive player root, hidden ones included.","lua_type":"{ BasePart }"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":120,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"IgnoreList","desc":"The raycast filter for a ray cast from the agent outwards: its entity alone, which\\n`FilterDescendantsInstances` extends to everything under it. The default `Ignore` of [Sight].","params":[{"name":"agent","desc":"","lua_type":"Agent"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`{ agent.Entity }`.","lua_type":"{ Instance }"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":132,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"PositionOf","desc":"Where the agent is: its mover\'s position when it has one, else its entity\'s pivot. The real\\n[Agent] has `GetPosition`; a spec\'s fake may not.","params":[{"name":"agent","desc":"","lua_type":"Agent"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":144,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"ModelOf","desc":"The Model a part belongs to, or `nil` when it has none or is a fake without\\n`FindFirstAncestorOfClass`. [Perception.CharacterOf] is the same lookup typed as a `Model`.","params":[{"name":"part","desc":"","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The nearest ancestor Model, or `nil`.","lua_type":"Instance?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":161,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"CharacterOf","desc":"The character a part belongs to. What a brain calls on `SeenTarget` or `NearestTarget` when\\nit wants the whole model rather than the root.","params":[{"name":"part","desc":"A root a sense wrote to the blackboard, or any part of a character.","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The nearest ancestor Model, or `nil` when there is none.","lua_type":"Model?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":178,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"HumanoidOf","desc":"The Humanoid a brain damages, checks the health of, or reads the state of, found through\\n[Perception.CharacterOf].","params":[{"name":"part","desc":"A root a sense wrote to the blackboard, or any part of a character.","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The Humanoid inside the part\'s character, or `nil` when there is no character or no Humanoid.","lua_type":"Humanoid?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":190,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"EyeOf","desc":"The part to look out of for a character. [Watched] judges an observer\'s look direction by\\nthis part\'s `CFrame`.","params":[{"name":"root","desc":"","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The character\'s `Head` when it has one, else `root` itself.","lua_type":"BasePart"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":212,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"RaycastParams","desc":"Raycast parameters that exclude `ignore` (and their descendants) and water.","params":[{"name":"ignore","desc":"Passed through, with their descendants.","lua_type":"{ Instance }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"RaycastParams"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":235,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"Transparent","desc":"Glass and fences: parts this transparent do not block sight.","params":[{"name":"threshold","desc":"`Transparency` at or above which a part is see-through. Default `0.5`.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"A `SeeThrough` predicate for [Perception.LineOfSight] and [Sight].","lua_type":"(part: BasePart) -> boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":264,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"LineOfSight","desc":"Is the straight line from `from` to `to` clear? `true` when the ray hits nothing, or hits\\n`allow` or something under it, which is how a target\'s own body does not block sight of it.\\nWithout `seeThrough`, anything else the ray hits blocks, glass included; pass\\n[Perception.Transparent] or your own rule to look past it.","params":[{"name":"from","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"to","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"ignore","desc":"What the ray passes through.","lua_type":"{ Instance }"},{"name":"allow","desc":"What the ray may hit and still count as clear, usually the target\'s own model.","lua_type":"Instance?"},{"name":"seeThrough","desc":"Parts this returns `true` for do not block; the ray is cast again past them, up to eight times.","lua_type":"((part: BasePart) -> boolean)?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":286,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"CountWalls","desc":"How many walls stand between a sound and a listener. [Hearing] and [Sounds] multiply the\\nloudness by `Occlusion` once per wall.","params":[{"name":"from","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"to","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"ignore","desc":"What does not count, with descendants: the listener\'s entity, the source\'s part.","lua_type":"{ Instance }"},{"name":"limit","desc":"Stop counting here. Default `3`.","lua_type":"number?"},{"name":"margin","desc":"Hits within this many studs of `to` do not count, so a noise inside a body is not walled off by that body. Default `2`.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"How many distinct parts the straight line crosses, up to `limit`.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":336,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"LightFalloff","desc":"","params":[{"name":"distance","desc":"Studs from the light.","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"range","desc":"The light\'s `Range`.","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"brightness","desc":"The light\'s `Brightness`.","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`brightness` at the light, falling linearly to `0` at `range`. Pure.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":382,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"LightContribution","desc":"Read duck-typed (`Enabled`, `Brightness`, `Range`, `Parent`, and for a spot light `Angle` and\\n`Face`), so a spec can pass a plain table.","params":[{"name":"light","desc":"A `PointLight`, `SpotLight` or `SurfaceLight` on a part or an attachment.","lua_type":"Light"},{"name":"position","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"}],"returns":[{"desc":"How much this light lights `position`: `0` when disabled, out of range, not on a part, or outside a spot light\'s cone.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":398,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"LightAt","desc":"How lit a spot is, from the lights tagged [Perception.LIGHT_TAG]. Tag the lights that matter\\nto the AI (a flashlight, the ceiling lamps, a fire) and pass this as a [Sight] `Visibility`,\\nand a player in the dark is invisible until a light finds them. Not physically accurate; a\\ngameplay number.","params":[{"name":"position","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"ambient","desc":"Light everywhere, added before the clamp. `0` is pitch black where no light reaches. Default `0`.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The light level at `position` in `[0, 1]`: `ambient` plus every tagged light\'s [Perception.LightContribution], clamped.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":456,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"SeenByAnyone","desc":"\\"Would anyone see it happen here?\\" The check to run before a stalker teleports, spawns or\\nvanishes, so it only ever does so off screen. The [Watched] sense is the same question asked\\nabout the agent every tick; this is the one-off version about any point.","params":[{"name":"position","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"options","desc":"","lua_type":"SeenByOptions?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`true` when any observer has `position` inside their view cone with a clear line to it.","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":498,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"InCone","desc":"Is `position` inside the cone that opens `fieldOfViewDegrees` wide around `origin.LookVector`,\\nwithin `range` studs? The angle is the true angle in three dimensions, so something high above\\nis outside just as something off to the side is. A position at the origin counts as inside.\\nThe dot is returned either way, so a consideration can score on it.","params":[{"name":"origin","desc":"The eye; its `LookVector` is the centre of the cone.","lua_type":"CFrame"},{"name":"position","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"fieldOfViewDegrees","desc":"The full angle of the cone.","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"range","desc":"Studs.","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Inside the cone and within range.","lua_type":"boolean"},{"desc":"The dot product between the look vector and the direction to `position`: `1` dead ahead, `0` beside, `-1` behind.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":543,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"SortByDistance","desc":"A new list of `parts`, nearest to `origin` first. Stable: parts at the same distance keep\\ntheir order. `parts` is not touched.","params":[{"name":"origin","desc":"","lua_type":"Vector3"},{"name":"parts","desc":"","lua_type":"{ BasePart }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"A new list, nearest first.","lua_type":"{ BasePart }"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":575,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}}],"properties":[{"name":"HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTE","desc":"The attribute name that hides a character from every sense: set it to `true` on the\\ncharacter (or on its root) while the player is in a locker, under a bed, or otherwise out of\\nthe game\'s sight rules, and [Perception.AliveRoots] leaves them out until it is cleared.","lua_type":"\\"AI_HIDDEN\\"","source":{"line":54,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}},{"name":"LIGHT_TAG","desc":"The `CollectionService` tag a light must carry for [Perception.LightAt] to count it.","lua_type":"\\"AI_LIGHT\\"","source":{"line":373,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}}],"types":[{"name":"SeenByOptions","desc":"","fields":[{"name":"FieldOfView","lua_type":"number?","desc":"The full angle of each observer\'s view cone. Default `100`."},{"name":"Range","lua_type":"number?","desc":"Studs. Default `math.huge`."},{"name":"Eye","lua_type":"((root: BasePart) -> CFrame?)?","desc":"Where an observer looks from. Default: the character\'s head, else its root ([Perception.EyeOf]). A game that replicates the camera returns it here."},{"name":"Ignore","lua_type":"{ Instance }?","desc":"What the sight ray passes through. Default nothing."},{"name":"Observers","lua_type":"{ BasePart }?","desc":"Who may be looking. Default [Perception.AllAliveRoots], hidden players included."}],"source":{"line":480,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}}],"name":"Perception","desc":"The helpers the built-in senses are made of, and the place to start when writing your own.\\nA [Types.Sense] is any table with `Tick`; the work inside one is usually \\"who could I be\\nlooking at\\" (`AliveRoots`), \\"is it in front of me\\" (`InCone`), \\"is anything in the way\\"\\n(`LineOfSight`), \\"which is nearest\\" (`SortByDistance`), and this module answers each of those\\non its own.\\n\\nEverything here is about *targets*: [Perception.HumanoidOf] takes a root a sense wrote to the\\nblackboard and finds that character\'s humanoid. The agent\'s own humanoid is\\n`agent.Entity:FindFirstChildOfClass(\\"Humanoid\\")`, and the two look alike in code, so name\\nthe variable.\\n\\n`Targets` on every built-in sense defaults to [Perception.AliveRoots], and `Ignore` on\\n[Sight] defaults to [Perception.IgnoreList]. A brain that acts on a target root a sense wrote\\nto the blackboard reaches the rest of the character through [Perception.CharacterOf] and\\n[Perception.HumanoidOf].\\n\\nEverything that takes a part reads it duck-typed, so a spec can pass plain tables.","source":{"line":42,"path":"lib/Senses/Perception.luau"}}')}}]);